  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is composed of three fundamental elements: chocolate, lemon, and strawberry. Here's a simplified guide:\n\n1. Melt 1 cup of chocolate in a heatproof bowl set over simmering water.\n2. While the chocolate is melting, construct a bowl for the lemon mixture.\n3. In a separately prepared container, blend 1 cup of lemon juice with 1 cup of water.\n4. Add 1 cup of strawberries, cut into small pieces, to the lemon mixture.\n5. Combine the melted chocolate with the lemon-strawberry mixture.\n6. Pour the mixture into a wooden container.\n7. Refrigerate the mixture until it is frozen solid.\n8. Serve as needed.\n\nNote: Chocolate may need to be added in portions according to personal preference. Enjoy your Neapolitan treat!",
